# Session handoff — local only, never committed
HANDOFF.md

# Terraform
**/.terraform/*
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
# Explicit rule (PX-018) — previously relied on ~/.gitignore_global for
# *.tfvars coverage, a personal machine-local file this repo can't
# enforce or guarantee exists on a fresh clone/CI/another machine.
# terraform.tfvars holds a real Proxmox API token.
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Ansible
*.retry
.vault_pass
.kubeconfig
# ansible.cfg's roles_path/collections cache — empty today, but nothing
# else stops git from picking up content here if it's ever populated.
.ansible/

# General
.DS_Store
*.swp
# .env is already covered by ~/.gitignore_global

# Python (landing/)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ruff_cache/

# JetBrains IDE
.idea/

# k8s/sealed-secrets/ is the Sealed Secrets *controller's* own Helm
# values (resource limits, no actual secret material) — it legitimately
# belongs in git. A personal global gitignore rule matching "*secrets*"
# was silently excluding this whole directory from every commit since
# PX-009 (caught in PX-013: a real pipeline run linted 8 of 9 charts,
# not 9, because this file had never actually been committed at all).
# Explicit override so a global rule can't silently swallow tracked
# project content again.
!k8s/sealed-secrets/
!k8s/sealed-secrets/**

# Same global "*secrets*" rule recurred (PX-015) for the ArgoCD
# Application manifest that adopts the controller above — no secret
# material here either, just an Application CR. Explicit override
# per-file rather than widening the pattern, since future files
# genuinely matching "*secrets*" (an actual sealed secret) should stay
# caught by other, more specific rules if any are ever added.
!k8s/argocd/apps/sealed-secrets.yaml

# Same class of bug again (PX-033): a personal global gitignore rule
# ("*.pub" — sensible in general, real SSH public keys shouldn't be
# committed) was silently excluding this one legitimate, non-sensitive
# test fixture (not a real key, content is never validated, just read
# and trimmed by a mocked Terraform test). Explicit per-file override
# rather than widening the pattern, since a real *.pub file landing
# here in the future should stay caught.
!terraform/tests/fixtures/mock-ssh-key.pub

# Third occurrence of the same "*.pub" gitignore gap (PX-034) — same
# reasoning, same per-file override rather than widening the pattern.
!ansible/roles/common/molecule/default/files/mock-ssh-key.pub
